# Build context exclusions for the shared service Dockerfile.
#
# The build context is the repository root, so anything not explicitly excluded
# here is uploaded to the Docker daemon on every build. That is slow, and it
# also means local secrets can end up inside an image layer.
#
# .env is excluded deliberately: it holds generated credentials, and a file
# that should never be copied into an image must never reach the build context
# in the first place. Context exclusion is defence in depth behind "the
# Dockerfile never COPYs it".

# ---- secrets: never let these reach the daemon
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.jks
**/secrets/**

# ---- VCS + IDE
.git
.gitignore
.github
.idea
*.iml
.vscode
.DS_Store

# ---- build output: the image builds from source inside the container
**/target/
**/build/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
*.class
*.jar
*.war

# ---- docs and local scripts: not needed to produce a jar
docs/
README.md
LICENSE
*.md
scripts/

# ---- observability state
infrastructure/prometheus/data/
infrastructure/grafana/data/
**/*.tsdb
